oun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349242">Biznes uchun Skype PSTN mahalliy qo‘ng‘iroqlari</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40431_2347755_2349243"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service plan offer covering international calls as part of the PSTN Calling service in Office 365.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2347755">Skype for Business PSTN International Calling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349243">Biznes uchun Skype PSTN xalqaro qo‘ng‘iroqlari</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40432_2347756_2349241"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The service plan offer covering domestic and international calls as part of the PSTN Calling service in Office 365.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2347756">Skype for Business PSTN Domestic and International Calling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349241">Biznes uchun Skype PSTN mahalliy va xalqaro qo‘ng‘iroqlari</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40436_2349281_2353033"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A menu item showing hearts (number of likes) for a given chat message. The heart-feature refers to giving and removing hearts and is distinct from the Like-feature known from e.g. Facebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349281">Show likes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353033">Yoqtirishlar soni</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40438_2349283_2353034"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A menu item connected the heart-feature, whereby a participant can remove a "heart" from a chat message, indicating that the participant does not like a chat message. The heart-feature refers to giving and removing hearts and is distinct from the Like-feature known from e.g. Facebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349283">Unlike</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353034">Yoqmadi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40439_2349284_2353030"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An amount of money added to an account.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349284">credit</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353030">kredit</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40440_2349285_2353031"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A menu item connected the heart-feature, whereby a participant can give a "heart" to a chat message, indicating that the participant likes a chat message. The heart-feature refers to giving and removing hearts and is distinct from the Like-feature known from e.g. Facebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349285">Like</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353031">Yoqdi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40441_2349286_2353032"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A list of hearts showing how many particpant have liked a chat message. The heart-feature refers to giving and removing hearts and is distinct from the Like-feature known from e.g. Facebook.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2349286">Likes</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2353032">Yoqtirganlar</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40454_3113359_3113868"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The security service that provides a consolidated view into risk events and potential vulnerabilities affecting your organization’s identities.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3113359">Microsoft Entra ID Protection</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3113868">Microsoft Entra ID’si himoyasi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40474_2350857_3025154"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A servicing release cadence to receive development builds. Each ring is defined by a different release frequency and level of stability.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2350857">ring</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="3025154">halqa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40475_2350858_2503922"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office servicing option in which new feature upgrades are available for installation right after they were first published by Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2350858">Current Branch</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2503922">Monthly Channel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40475_2350860_2503922"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office servicing option in which new feature upgrades are available for installation right after they were first published by Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2350860">CB</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2503922">Monthly Channel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="40475_2364917_2503922"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The Office servicing option in which new feature upgrades are available for installation right after they were first published by Microsoft.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2364917">Current Channel</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="uz-Latn"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2503922">Monthly Channel</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">UZB</termNote>